    "reviewNotes": "Only openspec was assigned; speckit was intentionally and correctly skipped per coordinator notes — this is a trivial hello-world story with no security, edge-case, or testability concerns warranting a second review. OpenSpec added meaningful value by identifying the precise fix site (the getGreeting function, not the test) and clarifying the requirement delta ('hello dolly' vs existing 'hello world'). Brownfield ticket with empty acceptance criteria — not evaluating AC elaboration or split quality per policy. No human review needed.",
    "qualityScore": 0.85,
